otes that A-FDT can diverge from policy-FDT, but since the inputs differ I'm treating the twin as separate, so I'll conclude that A-FDT says to submit the letter.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Under A-FDT, my node is fdt(P,G,x), keyed to my own input, while the other copy's action runs through fdt(P,G,x'), a different node, so intervening on mine shouldn't shift theirs unless G happens to encode that same function on the different input. I'm checking whether the essay's A-FDT only intervenes on the action.\n\nUnder A-FDT the twin's action sits on a different node, so the essay's rule of intervening only on the actual input leaves it as a prior, and defecting dominates for any q. The essay's section 6 notes that A-FDT can diverge from policy-FDT, but since the inputs differ I'm treating the twin as separate, so I'll conclude that A-FDT says to submit the letter.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9254,"completion_tokens":692,"total_tokens":9946,"cost":0.050856,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.050856,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.037016,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01384},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":324,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}